# composer/composer -- picked for the SOLVER. Nothing else measured here builds a
# graph and searches it: the dependency resolver is a long-running pure-PHP
# computation over hundreds of thousands of array operations, string comparisons and
# recursive structures, and its tests assert an exact solution rather than "no error".
# It is also the tool that installs every other project in this directory, so a wrong
# answer here is a wrong answer under the whole gate.
REPO="https://github.com/composer/composer.git"
# The pin tracks composer's own releases and NOT this box's installed composer, which
# is what produced the locks beside it. 2.10.2 was both, until its `diagnose` command
# started failing under the ORACLE: that command runs a LIVE audit of composer itself
# against packagist's advisory feed, so a published advisory against the pinned release
# reddens the step for a reason no engine can answer. 2.10.3 carries the fix. The step
# is world-coupled by construction and will red again on the next advisory -- the pin
# is the only lever, and it is an owner's.
REF="2.10.3"
# composer's own `test` script is `@php simple-phpunit`, and symfony/phpunit-bridge's
# simple-phpunit DOWNLOADS and installs a PHPUnit on first use. That install is a build
# step, not a measurement, so it runs once under the ORACLE; the steps below then run
# the installed PHPUnit under each engine in turn.
PREPARE='"$PHP_BIN" vendor/bin/simple-phpunit install'
# Three things differ between two runs of the SAME engine here, and all three reach
# the output: PHPUnit mints every mock's class name with a per-run hash
# (Mock_Runtime_b215996f) that a TypeError raised inside one prints, and Composer's
# own scratch directory and the target it extracts into carry fresh random names
# that one test quotes as part of the command line it failed to run.
NORMALIZE='s/Mock_\([A-Za-z0-9_]*\)_[0-9a-f]\{8\}/Mock_\1_@HASH@/g
s#composer-test-[0-9a-f]\{16,\}#composer-test-@TMP@#g
s#composer-test-@TMP@/composer/[0-9a-f]\{8\}\b#composer-test-@TMP@/composer/@DIR@#g
s#composer-test-@TMP@/composer/tmp-[0-9a-f]\{32\}#composer-test-@TMP@/composer/tmp-@NAME@#g'
# The suite is 17s under php and roughly 7 minutes under phl on this box, so the
# 600s default budget is inside the noise of a loaded machine rather than above it.
# A timeout here would be read as a divergence, which is exactly the wrong answer.
STEP_TIMEOUT=1800
